{"kind":"event","event_id":10179,"event_uid":"01M2R388B5NE9EEH58RVNT266B","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":33,"project_uid":"01M2HSJCAB4WXJ7C6XEG23B869","project_name":"popmechanic-tinyapp-fixture","issue_id":409,"issue_uid":"01M2R3212DY5M5G2F7HYWZDMGC","issue_short_id":"dmgc","actor":"impl:1@run-34","hlc_physical_ms":1789662601573,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"04543fc4abfa50c5f532a9aaf068b151d9169db0784a207917fe79aa92376272","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2R388B4NTKFBSEB1DKW5DDB","author":"impl:1@run-34","body":"Task 1 approach: lift server/test/celld.ts into packages/tinyapp-exam/src/celld.ts as startCelld({serverDir, exam, budgetMb?, readyMs?}) -> {url, ws, dir, port, stop} (plus argv/env on the result and an onSpawn option, so leg (a) can pin the spawn argv/env without a probe binary), adding the two rejections BASE never had: exit-before-ready (code + stderr) and readyMs timeout (message names readyMs, process killed). New src/surface.ts carries examSurface(url) with content/rows/fork/reload/discard/events plus a generic call(verb, params) for leg (d)'s 404 case; fork dials <ws>/sync/<to> and hangs up first so the module object learns its name from the root's x-tinyapp-module header before the seed transition (run-33's finding: leg (d)'s module clause is satisfiable and gets pinned). Then delete server/test/celld.ts and re-point the two server tests' imports at 'tinyapp-exam', keeping their child-process form.","created_at":"2026-09-17T16:30:01.572175767Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-17T16:30:01.573Z"}
