{"kind":"event","event_id":10181,"event_uid":"01M2R39E03EP7HDVGJBS0RQTV2","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":33,"project_uid":"01M2HSJCAB4WXJ7C6XEG23B869","project_name":"popmechanic-tinyapp-fixture","issue_id":409,"issue_uid":"01M2R3212DY5M5G2F7HYWZDMGC","issue_short_id":"dmgc","actor":"exam:1@run-34","hlc_physical_ms":1789662640131,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"c1f4bd6edbc1ee24986a452af4e8f320cec7cb4f819c4ca1484d6a60a39e3099","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2R39E014S9WETQPW8CNFX6Q","author":"exam:1@run-34","body":"examiner (round 2, run-34), approach for packages/tinyapp-exam/test/celld.test.ts:\n\n- Import `startCelld`/`examSurface` from the package name `tinyapp-exam` (M1/M3 say the package exports them; at BASE the named import is missing, which is the one red reason).\n- Leg (a): two real runtimes (exam:false, exam:true) for `/` containing `root`, `/exam/content?f=todos` 404 vs 200 + `[{},{}]`, and `.dev.vars` absent/`TINYAPP_EXAM=1`; argv and env pinned by the probe-binary route the leg allows — a per-call shell script named through CELLD_BIN that writes argv, CELLD_ESBUILD, CELLD_MAX_RSS_MB and the copy-list listing of its dir argument to a file baked into the script text (no reliance on env inheritance, no reliance on an undeclared export).\n- Leg (b): stderr `boom`/exit 3 script; and a `exec sleep` script recording its own pid, readyMs 1500, message contains 1500, pid gone (checked through /proc, zombie counted as gone).\n- Leg (c): stop() on a running instance — port re-bindable, dir gone, under 15 s.\n- Leg (d): as the run-33 finding settles it — the `module` half is pinned, not declared unsatisfiable: open `events`, fork `todos -> todos@y`, and assert over the subset of delivered messages whose `module` equals `todos@y` (other modules share the socket), with a numeric `seq`. The priming `/sync/<to>` dial inside `fork` is the implementer's business; the exam asserts only the outcome.\n- Leg (e): the exam encodes the three static halves (server/test/celld.ts absent, both server tests importing from 'tinyapp-exam'). The fourth Run line (`bun test` over those two) stays the driver's Run line — an exam never runs another package's tests.\n\nNext: reconnaissance against a real celld to confirm the `module: 'todos@y'` transition is observable with a priming dial before writing the file.","created_at":"2026-09-17T16:30:40.129869436Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-17T16:30:40.131Z"}
